{
  "_note": [
    "findings.md §1 measures exactly one row here: `feeds/videos.xml?channel_id=` answered",
    "200 with 39 KB in 0.35 s. That is the Atom case, and it is the only route this adapter",
    "declares.",
    "",
    "`podcast_rss.xml` is the other half of the roster row — RSS 2.0, enclosures, and",
    "podcast transcript links — and it is a parser proof rather than a route proof. No route",
    "this package declares is known to send a document of that shape. The reopen condition",
    "is measuring a podcast feed and adding a route constant for it; until then the honest",
    "claim is that the parser reads RSS 2.0 correctly, not that this package fetches one."
  ],
  "cases": [
